<br/>
Civil war continues on Kolgujev, with the Kolgujev Independence Forces (KIF) engaged against the Kolgujev Armed Forces (KAF).
NATO backs the Independence Forces, while Russia backs the KAF. To date, foreign involvement on both sides has been limited to supplies and training.
<br/><br/>
Two weeks ago, a small KIF element succeeded in destroying the KAF's artillery assets and eliminating a high-value target believed to be the KAF commander.
The element was subsequently wiped out in a large-scale retaliatory offensive launched by the KAF.
Worse still, intelligence on Commander Viktor Sudakov proved faulty: the actual KAF commander, General Medvedev, was not present during the strike.
<br/><br/>
The KAF have since seized a significant portion of the country and have just completed construction of a new FOB in a forested area near the current front line.
Intelligence indicates that General Medvedev is presently visiting this FOB. Capturing him offers an opportunity to end the conflict before it escalates further.
<br/><br/>
NATO has tasked the USMC with deploying a small team to Kolgujev to carry out this mission.
<br/><br/>
